## Find the angle at O in triangle ROP
The angles in triangle $ROP$ add to $180^\circ$.
|\angle POR| &= 180 - 87 - 88
&= 5^\circ
## Use the sine rule to find |RO|
$|RO|$ is opposite the $87^\circ$ angle and $|RP| = 20$ is opposite the $5^\circ$ angle.
\frac{|RO|}{\sin 87^\circ} &= \frac{20}{\sin 5^\circ}
|RO| &= \frac{20\sin 87^\circ}{\sin 5^\circ}
&= 229.16\ \text{m}
## Use tangent in triangle ROH to find |OH|
The angle of elevation at $R$ is $17^\circ$, and $|OH|$ is opposite it.
\tan 17^\circ &= \frac{|OH|}{|RO|}
|OH| &= |RO| \tan 17^\circ
&= 229.16 \times \tan 17^\circ
&\approx 70\ \text{m}
ANSWER: |OH| = 70\ \text{m}

## Find the total who played on all three days
These are the four 3rd June PLAY boxes.
186624 + 12960 + 12960 + 900 &= 213444
## Find those who lost on 1st or 2nd June (or both)
This is everyone except the win-then-win path, so leave out $186624$.
12960 + 12960 + 900 &= 26820
## Find the probability
P &= \frac{26820}{213444}
&= \frac{745}{5929}
ANSWER: \frac{745}{5929}

## Find the area of one of the 6 triangles
The hexagon splits into 6 congruent equilateral triangles of side $x$.
\text{Area of one triangle} &= \frac{140}{6}
&= \frac{70}{3}
## Write the triangle area using the area formula
Area $= \frac12 ab\sin C$, with $a = b = x$ and $C = 60^\circ$.
\frac{1}{2}x^2 \sin 60^\circ &= \frac{70}{3}
\frac{1}{2}x^2 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} &= \frac{70}{3}
\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}x^2 &= \frac{70}{3}
## Solve for x squared
x^2 &= \frac{70}{3} \times \frac{4}{\sqrt{3}}
x^2 &= \frac{280}{3\sqrt{3}}
## Take the positive square root and round
A length is positive, so we take the positive root.
x &= \sqrt{\frac{280}{3\sqrt{3}}}
&\approx 7.34
&\approx 7.3
ANSWER: x = 7.3\text{ cm}

## Find |AC| using the right-angled triangle ACD
$|\angle ADC| = 90^\circ$, so $\cos\alpha = \frac{|AD|}{|AC|}$.
\frac{8}{|AC|} &= \frac{7}{8}
|AC| &= \frac{8 \times 8}{7}
|AC| &= \frac{64}{7}
## Find |CD| using Pythagoras in triangle ACD
|CD| &= \sqrt{|AC|^2 - |AD|^2}
|CD| &= \sqrt{\left(\frac{64}{7}\right)^2 - 8^2}
&= \sqrt{\frac{4096}{49} - \frac{3136}{49}}
&= \sqrt{\frac{960}{49}}
&= \frac{8\sqrt{15}}{7}
## Find the area of triangle ACD
The right angle is at $D$, so base $|AD|$ and height $|CD|$.
\text{Area}(ACD) &= \frac{1}{2}(8)\left(\frac{8\sqrt{15}}{7}\right)
&= \frac{32\sqrt{15}}{7}
## Double it, since ABCD is symmetrical about AC
\text{Area}(ABCD) &= 2 \times \frac{32\sqrt{15}}{7}
&= \frac{64\sqrt{15}}{7}
&\approx 35.410
&\approx 35.41
ANSWER: \text{Area} = 35.41\text{ cm}^2

## Find the tangent at P
The radius $OP$ lies along the $x$-axis, so the tangent at $P(-1, 0)$ is vertical.
x &= -1
## Find the slope of the tangent at Q
The tangent is perpendicular to the radius $OQ$.
m_{OQ} &= \frac{\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} - 0}{-\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} - 0}
&= -1
m_{\text{tangent}} &= 1
## Write the equation of the tangent at Q
Use $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$ with $Q\left(-\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}, \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right)$.
y - \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} &= 1\left(x + \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right)
y &= x + \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
y &= x + \frac{2}{\sqrt{2}}
y &= x + \sqrt{2}
## Find the centre, where the two tangents meet
The centre lies on both tangents, so put $x = -1$ into $y = x + \sqrt{2}$.
y &= -1 + \sqrt{2}
\text{Centre} &= (-1,\ -1 + \sqrt{2})
## Find the radius
$P(-1, 0)$ is on $s$ and sits directly below the centre, so the radius is the distance from the centre to $P$.
r &= (-1 + \sqrt{2}) - 0
r &= -1 + \sqrt{2}
ANSWER: \text{Centre} = (-1,\ -1 + \sqrt{2}),\quad \text{Radius} = -1 + \sqrt{2}

## Use the modulus formula
For $z = a + bi$, $|z| = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$. Here $z_3 = 6 - 2i$, so $a = 6$ and $b = -2$.
|z_3| &= \sqrt{6^2 + (-2)^2}
## Evaluate under the root
&= \sqrt{36 + 4}
&= \sqrt{40}
## Write in surd form
$40 = 4 \times 10$ and $\sqrt{4} = 2$.
&= \sqrt{4 \times 10}
&= 2\sqrt{10}
ANSWER: \sqrt{40} = 2\sqrt{10}
